15:["$","ul","b946-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b946",{"children":[["$","strong","b944",{"children":["The agent is the headline, and the soft spot. "]}],"On paper FAUNA is a full canvas agent. In practice, reviewers and users report it often needs correcting on multi-step briefs, and it lives only in the browser tab, no Slack, no concurrent agents, no team-taught skills. It exists; the question is how much it actually carries."]}],["$","li","b949",{"children":[["$","strong","b947",{"children":["A steep learning curve. "]}],"Flora explicitly targets teams comfortable with node-based systems, and reviewers suggest investing a full day before you're productive, even if you already know Figma."]}],["$","li","b952",{"children":[["$","strong","b950",{"children":["A canvas that stalls as it grows. "]}],"Flora is fine on small graphs, but teams report it bogging down as a project scales, well before the node counts a real multi-scene campaign reaches, so the canvas becomes the ceiling."]}],["$","li","b955",{"children":[["$","strong","b953",{"children":["Files to browse, not assets to search. "]}],"Flora keeps your outputs in a file library, but there's no semantic search, so finding the shot you made last week means scrolling, not describing it."]}]]}]
