2f:["$","td","b10392",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b1048",{"children":["Saved styles / per-turn refs"]}]]}]
30:["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]
31:["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. Flora is the product from Florafauna (florafauna.ai), and its built-in agent is named FAUNA. When people compare a Flora alternative, they mean this node-based canvas. Melius is the closest like-for-like: a node canvas plus an agent, but with an agent that also runs in Slack and concurrently, a gentler learning curve, and one shared credit pool."}]
32:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is Melius easier to learn than Flora?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"It aims to be. Flora is explicitly pitched at technical teams comfortable with node systems, and reviewers suggest budgeting a full day before you're productive. Melius keeps the same node power but lets Mel build and wire the graph from a brief, so you can steer in plain language instead of assembling every node by hand."}]]}]
33:["$","details","5",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can Melius handle video work?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. Melius routes to frontier video models and includes an in-app multi-track editor to assemble the result. Because every model shares one credit pool, you can compare a shot across Kling, Veo and Seedance without juggling separate budgets."}]]}]
35:["$","$L34","post-figma-weave-alternative",{"post":{"_key":"post-figma-weave-alternative","slug":"figma-weave-alternative","category":"comparisons","title":"The best Figma Weave alternative for generative design","isoDate":"2026-07-21","date":"July 21, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Looking for a Figma Weave (Weavy) alternative? Weave puts a generation canvas next to your design files, great if you live in Figma. If you don't, the ecosystem coupling and fast credit burn become constraints. Here's how Melius compares as a standalone, canvas-first workspace with an agent and one credit pool.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/figma-weave-alternative/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best Figma Weave alternative?","answer":"Melius is the strongest standalone alternative to Figma Weave. Both are node-based generation canvases with broad model access, but Melius is an independent creative workspace rather than a layer tied to the Figma ecosystem, it adds Mel to plan and wire multi-step work, and it keeps every model under one credit pool."},{"question":"How is Melius different from Figma Weave?","answer":"The biggest difference is the agent. Figma Weave has no AI agent, so its node graphs are wired and run by hand, and it is deeply tied to Figma's ecosystem. Melius is a standalone, agent-first workspace: Mel builds and runs the graph from a brief and also works in Slack, its MCP is canvas-level so an external agent like Claude can drive the canvas from any host, and every model shares one subscription."},{"question":"Is Figma Weave the same as Weavy?","answer":"Yes. Weavy was the original node-based generation canvas; Figma acquired it and rebranded it Figma Weave, folding it into Figma Design. So a Weavy alternative and a Figma Weave alternative are the same search. If you want that node-canvas-plus-generation model but without the Figma coupling, Melius is a standalone equivalent with an agent and one shared credit pool."},{"question":"Why do people look for a Figma Weave alternative?","answer":"The dominant complaint is credit cost: users report credits burning extremely fast, sometimes thousands of credits for a few minutes of work, with iterative fixes for AI mistakes eating more. There are also reports of billing friction on cancellation, and some tooling is still in open beta. Teams outside the Figma ecosystem also want a standalone option."},{"question":"Does Melius integrate with design tools?","answer":"Melius exposes an MCP server, so an agent like Claude can read and act on your canvas from your own environment. Rather than binding generation to one design suite, it aims to be model-agnostic and host-agnostic so it fits whatever workflow you already use."},{"question":"Can Melius sequence video like Weave's Timeline?","answer":"Yes. Melius includes an in-app multi-track editor for arranging shots, timing and layering audio, alongside the node canvas for building the generations that feed it."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"what-figma-weave-does-well","title":"What Weave does well"},{"_key":"where-teams-hit-friction","title":"The friction"},{"_key":"how-melius-approaches-the-same-work","title":"The Melius approach"},{"_key":"who-should-switch","title":"Who should switch"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1179","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1178","text":"Figma Weave, the product that started as Weavy before Figma acquired it, is a strong idea: a node-based generation canvas with real editing tools, compositing, masking, color grading, and a Timeline for sequencing, plus a set of one-click workflows surfaced right inside Figma Design. For designers who already live in Figma, having generation that close to their work is compelling.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1183","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1180","text":"That tight coupling is also the reason people search for a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1181","text":"Figma Weave alternative","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1182","text":". If you don't live in Figma, or you want a standalone workspace with an agent and more predictable costs, the ecosystem fit becomes a constraint rather than a feature. Here's how Melius compares.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1185","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1184","text":"What Figma Weave does well","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-figma-weave-does-well"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1187","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1186","text":"Weave combines generation with genuine editing, compositing, masking and grading, not just prompt-in, image-out, and its node graph makes each step visible and re-runnable. The June 2026 Timeline brought video sequencing and sound onto the same canvas, and the embedded workflows make common design tasks a click away for anyone already in Figma. As a design-adjacent generation layer, it's well built.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1189","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1188","text":"Where teams hit friction","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-teams-hit-friction"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1192","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1190","text":"No agent, fully manual. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1191","text":"This is the biggest gap. Where the rest of the field has some kind of AI agent, Weave's node graphs are wired and run by hand, so someone has to build every pipeline. There's also no announced Slack, MCP, API or CLI to drive it from elsewhere.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1195","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1193","text":"Credits burn fast. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1194","text":"A dominant complaint: users report thousands of credits consumed for a few minutes of work, with iterative fixes for AI mistakes, effectively paying to troubleshoot the tool, eating still more.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1198","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1196","text":"Ecosystem lock-in. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1197","text":"Weave's value is tightly coupled to Figma's world, and there's no audio or voice. If your team isn't Figma-first, much of the advantage doesn't apply.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1201","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1199","text":"Mid-acquisition uncertainty. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1200","text":"Some embedded tooling and the full Figma-to-Weave sync are still rolling out through beta, so the roadmap is moving while Figma folds it in.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1203","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1202","text":"How Melius approaches the same work","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-melius-approaches-the-same-work"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1205","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1204","text":"Melius is a standalone, agent-first workspace, so the thing Weave leaves to you, building and running the graph, is exactly what the agent does.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1208","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1206","text":"An agent instead of manual wiring. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1207","text":"Mel reads your brief, picks a model per step, wires the node graph, runs it, and writes each per-model prompt, so multi-step work starts from intent, not hand assembly. It also runs in Slack and can carry your brand context and skills into every generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1211","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1209","text":"Drivable from your own tools. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1210","text":"A canvas-level MCP means an external agent like Claude can build and run the Melius canvas from your own environment, rather than binding your generations to a single design suite. Several agents can also work one canvas at once with visible presence.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1217","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b1214","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1212","text":"Generation, audio and assembly in one place. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1213","text":"Image, video and audio models (including voice and music) live on the same canvas, with an in-app multi-track editor to sequence and export, all under ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1215","text":"a single subscription","marks":["b1214"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1216","text":" with up to 8 seats on self-serve plans, unlimited seats on Enterprise, and unlimited agent usage.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1220","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1218","text":"Real-time multiplayer for the team. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1219","text":"A whole team works the same canvas live, without depending on one design ecosystem's rollout schedule.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1223","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1221","text":"Assets you can actually find. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1222","text":"Every generation and upload lands in a semantic asset library you search by what's in the image, not a flat pile of files to scroll through later.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b1224","rows":[{"_key":"b1225","cells":[{"_key":"b1226","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1228","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1227","text":"","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b1229","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1231","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1230","text":"Melius","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b1232","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1234","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1233","text":"Figma Weave","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1235","cells":[{"_key":"b1236","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1238","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1237","text":"Node-based canvas","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1239","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1241","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1240","text":"Yes","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1242","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1244","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1243","text":"Yes","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1245","cells":[{"_key":"b1246","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1248","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1247","text":"AI agent","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1249","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1251","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1250","text":"Operates the canvas + Slack","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1252","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1254","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1253","text":"None, fully manual","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1255","cells":[{"_key":"b1256","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1258","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1257","text":"Standalone or tied","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1259","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1261","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1260","text":"Standalone workspace","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1262","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1264","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1263","text":"Coupled to Figma ecosystem","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1265","cells":[{"_key":"b1266","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1268","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1267","text":"Drive from other tools","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1269","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1271","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1270","text":"Canvas-level MCP, any host","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1272","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1274","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1273","text":"None announced","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1275","cells":[{"_key":"b1276","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1278","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1277","text":"Audio / voice","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1279","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1281","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1280","text":"Voice, music & speech-to-text","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1282","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1284","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1283","text":"None","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b1285","cells":[{"_key":"b1286","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1288","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1287","text":"Pixel editing depth","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1289","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1291","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1290","text":"Growing","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b1292","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b1294","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1293","text":"Deepest in class (a real strength)","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1296","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1295","text":"Who should switch","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"who-should-switch"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1298","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1297","text":"If your team is Figma-first and mostly wants the deepest pixel editing next to your design files, Weave's editing and integration are a real advantage. If you want an agent that builds and runs the pipeline for you rather than wiring every node by hand, drivable from your own AI tools, with audio and one subscription across every model, Melius is the more independent, agent-first home for that work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1303","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b1300","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1299","text":"Work on a canvas that isn't locked to one tool. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1301","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b1300"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b1302","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b1305","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b1304","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b1306","items":"$35:props:post:faq"}]}}]
36:["$","$L34","post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp",{"post":{"_key":"post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","slug":"connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","category":"modus-news","title":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas with MCP","isoDate":"2026-07-20","date":"July 20, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas over MCP and skip the context drift you get from copy-pasting into a chatbot. The Model Context Protocol exposes the Melius canvas as live, structured data an agent can read and act on. Here is how to connect Claude to Melius, what the tools actually are, and why the loop self-corrects.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the Model Context Protocol (MCP)?","answer":"MCP is an open standard that lets an AI agent connect to a server and call the tools and resources that server exposes. It started with IDEs and terminals, and the same pattern lets an agent read and act on a live creative canvas instead of a screenshot."},{"question":"What is Claude MCP?","answer":"Claude MCP just means using the Model Context Protocol with Claude as the host: Claude connects to an MCP server and calls the tools it exposes. Point it at the Melius connector and Claude can read and act on your live canvas directly, rather than working from a pasted description. The protocol is host-agnostic, so any MCP-compatible model works the same way."},{"question":"How do I connect Claude to Melius?","answer":"The recommended path is the hosted connector. Add a custom MCP connector in your host and point it at https://mcp.melius.com/mcp, then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. Melius mints a durable, revocable connector key for that team, so there is nothing to paste and nothing to refresh."},{"question":"Does the agent generate the images and video itself?","answer":"No. The host model (for example Claude) is the agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do. The images, video, and audio are produced by the generation models available on the platform, selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate."},{"question":"Can I use a model other than Claude?","answer":"Yes. Because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any MCP-compatible host. Melius is model-agnostic at the host level."},{"question":"What stops the agent from acting on nodes that no longer exist?","answer":"The platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas, so if it references something that is no longer there, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work","title":"The MCP bridge"},{"_key":"connecting-claude-to-melius","title":"Connecting Claude"},{"_key":"a-self-correcting-loop","title":"Self-correcting loop"},{"_key":"bring-your-own-model","title":"Bring your own model"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b717","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b714","text":"When you work with a large language model in a creative environment, the most common point of failure isn't the model's reasoning, it's the data it can see. Many workflows still rely on a copy-paste style, where a person describes a canvas, a prompt, or a generated result to a chatbot by hand. That inevitably leads to ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b715","text":"context drift","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b716","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b721","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b718","text":"Context drift is when an agent's understanding of a project diverges from the actual state of the work over time. Standard LLM chats are stateless and disconnected from the tool's live state, so the agent loses track of which nodes exist, how they're wired, and which generation produced which output. It might ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b719","text":"remember","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b720","text":" a video node from three prompts ago with no way of knowing it was since deleted, re-run with a different model, or rewired to a new source image. Without a protocol-level bridge, the model stays blind and you become the manual data translator.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b723","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b722","text":"A standard bridge for creative work","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b732","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b725","href":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b724","text":"Can a standard protocol close the gap between creative software and external AI models? The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b726","text":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)","marks":["b725"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b727","text":" helps by defining an open interface that lets an agent connect to a server and call its exposed ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b728","text":"tools","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b729","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b730","text":"resources","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b731","text":". The developer community first adopted MCP to connect LLMs to IDEs and terminals, but the same pattern applies to creative software: expose the workspace as structured, queryable data instead of a flat screenshot.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b740","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b733","text":"Melius does exactly this. Its canvas is organized as Team â†’ Projects â†’ Canvas â†’ Nodes + Edges â†’ Runs. A canvas is a 2D workspace; ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b734","text":"nodes","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b735","text":" are creative units (text prompts, images, videos, audio, files); ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b736","text":"edges","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b737","text":" wire nodes together to pass data between them; and a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b738","text":"run","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b739","text":" executes AI generation on a node, taking its prompt, model config, and upstream inputs and producing an output. Over MCP, an agent reads that live node-and-edge graph and acts on it directly, rather than guessing from a description.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b742","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b741","text":"Connecting Claude to Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"connecting-claude-to-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b749","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b746","href":"https://docs.melius.com/mcp/overview","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b743","text":"Connecting takes a couple of minutes. The quickest path is the hosted connector: add a custom MCP connector in your host, point it at ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b744","text":"https://mcp.melius.com/mcp","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b745","text":", then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. For the full walkthrough, including the local server for development and how credentials work, see the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b747","text":"Melius MCP docs","marks":["b746"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b748","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b751","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b750","text":"What the agent can actually do","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b753","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b752","text":"Once connected, the host gets a focused set of capabilities that mirror how the canvas works, rather than one opaque API. At a high level, an agent can:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b756","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b754","text":"Read the live canvas","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b755","text":": what's on it, how the pieces are wired together, and each one's current output, all from the same live state your browser sees","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b757","text":"Understand what's possible","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b758","text":": which generation models are available and what each one needs, so it works from real capabilities instead of guessing","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b762","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b760","text":"Compose the work","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b761","text":": add, arrange, and wire together the pieces of a creative pipeline","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b765","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b763","text":"Run and follow through","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b764","text":": kick off generations and act on the results as they come back","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b772","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b769","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b766","text":"So a prompt like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b767","text":"generate a product shot, then animate it into a 5-second clip","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b768","text":" becomes a short pipeline the agent assembles and runs on the real canvas, not a visual approximation. It is the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b770","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b769"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b771","text":" driven from your own agent. The exact shape of that surface is where a lot of the craft lives, so we'll leave the finer mechanics to the platform.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b774","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b773","text":"A self-correcting loop","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-self-correcting-loop"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b776","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b775","text":"One genuinely useful property falls out of exposing the canvas as structured data: the platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas. If it references something that no longer exists, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state. A common failure mode, an agent confidently referencing something that isn't there, becomes a caught error and a re-scan, so the agent corrects itself instead of silently producing broken or failed work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b778","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b777","text":"Bring your own model","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"bring-your-own-model"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b782","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b779","text":"Melius is model-agnostic at the host level: because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any compatible host. Keep the two ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b780","text":"models","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b781","text":" in play distinct. The host model is the reasoning agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do; the generation models, the ones that actually produce images, video, and audio, are the ones available on the platform and selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b787","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b784","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b783","text":"By connecting the Melius MCP server, you aren't bolting on a black-box AI button, you're giving an external agent live, structured access to your canvas, so it has the context it needs to be genuinely useful. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b785","text":"Start creating with Melius","marks":["b784"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b786","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b789","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b788","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b790","items":"$36:props:post:faq"}]}}]
